  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the highest-priority task is to establish a clean, interpretable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest and most standard configuration: RNA is the primary modality in cellular profiling, PCA is the most widely used and interpretable dimensionality-reduction encoder, and singleprofile is the minimal profile setting. This experiment will give a reference validation accuracy/F1 for the RNA-only, single-profile case. Every subsequent experiment—image-only baselines, multiprofile variants, alternative encoders (scvi, scgpt), and multimodal fusion—can be meaningfully compared against this anchor. Without this baseline, performance differences from more complex configurations would be uninterpretable. Under a limited budget, spending the first experiment on the simplest, most informative baseline maximizes the information gained per experiment and sets the stage for efficient exploration of the remaining design dimensions."
}

